From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:29:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Import the AROS v1 port changes unchanged

Origin: aros-development-team/ports 93bdd123b7440881befe399b48a8fd4db5cd4f32,
  graphics/photocraft/photocraft-0.7.0-aros.diff, added there by commit
  8a6faee121308276c74493da23fe418b37c01f78 (Git author: Nick Andrews).
Problem: PhotoCraft's desktop shell (eframe/winit/wgpu) has no AROS backend,
  and the v1 port needs AROS path, font-directory and feature changes.
Rationale: start from the reviewed reference port exactly as published so
  that every later difference is a visible, separate patch. Several hunks are
  revised later (MCP/Tokio features, the plain-std::fs fallback).
Scope: all targets compile it; behaviour changes are cfg(target_os = "aros")
  or behind the new ui-egui `eframe` and automation `mcp`/`sandbox` features.
Upstream-status: local-only (import of the AROS ports recipe; not ours to send).
Prerequisites: none (applies to c450e755aed5e77fa6d4de7f04996085f5871085).
Verification: applied with patch -p1 without fuzz; built for x86_64 ABIv11.
Removal: when upstream PhotoCraft carries an equivalent shell split.
